  "id": "Compound::DB00972 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Adequate evidence from the visible paths suggests a potential mechanistic link between Azelastine and Cyp2e1, mediated through Cyp2a6 and Cyp2c19. Azelastine binds to Cyp2a6 and Cyp2c19, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes participate in the epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities that ultimately lead to the activation of Cyp2e1. The shared involvement of these enzymes in arachidonic acid metabolism implies that Azelastine may modulate Cyp2e1 activity through a common pathway. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a potential role for Azelastine in influencing Cyp2e1 function, particularly in the context of arachidonic acid metabolism.",
